# Hylda's Crown of Winter: "{1}, {T}: Tap target creature. This ability costs {1} less to activate during your turn" (CR 601.2f, 602.2b, 118.7a).
# Bot1 casts the Crown on turn 1 with three Moxen, so on turn 2 (Bot2's turn), with the Crown untapped but no mana source untapped, the ability (still {1} there)
# is not offered. On turn 3 (Bot1's turn) Bot1 plays an Island and does not use the Crown. On turn 4 (Bot2's turn) it costs {1}: Bot1 taps the Island for it and
# taps Bot2's Llanowar Elves, leaving the pool empty. On turn 5 (Bot1's turn) the Crown has untapped and the ability costs {0}: it is activated with an empty pool,
# taps the Elves again, and the Island stays untapped.

